<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Guard (Panama)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1953">1953</a>–<a href="/years/1983">1983</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Guardia Nacional</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National Guard (Guardia Nacional) was Panama's armed force, created in 1953 from the National Police. In 1968 it overthrew President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnulfo-arias">Arnulfo Arias</a>, and its commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omar-torrijos">Omar Torrijos</a> ruled the country and negotiated the Torrijos-Carter Treaties of 1977 for the canal's transfer. In 1983 it became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panamanian-defense-forces">Panama Defence Forces</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-noriega">Manuel Noriega</a> and was dissolved after the US invasion of 1989.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/national-guard-panama.jpg" alt="National Guard (Panama)" width="320" height="354" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SVG-image-maker · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Panama_(1925-1941,_1946-2006).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
